        "self_reported": {
          "assumptions": [
            "The brief's 'refused before running, even with --run' list applies with or without --run: a block that would be refused is never reported ok, so an unfilled scaffold shown without --run is exit 1, not 0.",
            "'--out writes the paste-back when the run produced one' means when the run is ok: an unverified block is never written to the operator's file.",
            "bash is on the reviewer's PATH (the suite and validation.sh run real probes); the tests have no fallback without it."
          ],
          "judgment_calls": [
            "The seam signature: run(argv, *, cwd, stdin, timeout, env, stdout_cap) -> RunResult(argv, exit_code, stdout, stderr, timed_out, stdout_capped, stderr_truncated, duration_seconds); env and stdout_cap added to the brief's list so handlers pass ctx.env and the cap is enforced while reading, not after.",
            "Stdout cap 262144 bytes (256 KiB), about seven times the largest recorded probe output; passing it kills the group at once rather than draining until the timeout.",
            "The process group is killed when the script itself exits, not only on timeout, so nothing a probe backgrounded outlives the run or holds the pipes.",
            "bash gets the script as `bash -c <script> twine-probe-<slug>` with stdin /dev/null: no temp file (the only write is --out), and a probe reading stdin cannot eat its own script.",
